# Non-boolean condition rejected

Verifies an `if` condition must produce the configured boolean type: an integer
literal is rejected before execution with the standard type diagnostic.

>>> source
if (1) {
    print(1)
}

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: if condition must produce `bool`, found `int64` at Span { start: 4, end: 5 }

<<< exit
1
